  "slug": "ringo-starr",
  "title": "Ringo Starr – songs, albums, biography, photos and more!",
  "date": null,
  "content": "<div class=\"breadcrumbs\" typeof=\"BreadcrumbList\" vocab=\"https://schema.org/\">\n<span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><a property=\"item\" typeof=\"WebPage\" title=\"Go to Beatle people.\" href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/\" class=\"post post-page\"><span property=\"name\">Beatle people</span></a><meta property=\"position\" content=\"1\"></span> » <span property=\"itemListElement\" typeof=\"ListItem\"><span property=\"name\" class=\"post post-page current-item\">Ringo Starr</span><meta property=\"url\" content=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/ringo-starr/\"><meta property=\"position\" content=\"2\"></span></div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><blockquote><div>I had this dream at 13 to play drums, nothing else, play drums. And when I got to play the drums, when I finally got a set when I was nearly 18, I wanted to play with good people and I started playing with the best band at the time, and then the next best band and then the biggest band, the best band of all.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Ringo Starr</div><p></p><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Starr_1\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Starr_2\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div class=\"content-column one_third\"><div id=\"Index_Starr_3\" class=\"widgets_on_page wop_tiny1  wop_small1  wop_medium1  wop_large1  wop_wide1\"><ul></ul></div></div><div style=\"clear: both;\"></div><p></p><div id=\"mediavine-settings\" data-blocklist-content-desktop=\"1\"></div></div><div style=\"font-size: 12px; margin: 10px 0 10px 0;\"><strong>Published:</strong> <time itemprop=\"datePublished\" datetime=\"2008-03-14T15:40:07+00:00\" content=\"2008-03-14T15:40:07+00:00\">14 March 2008 </time> | <time itemprop=\"dateModified\" datetime=\"2025-09-05T17:43:34+01:00\" content=\"2025-09-05T17:43:34+01:00\"><strong>Last updated:</strong> 5 September 2025</time></div><h2>Biography</h2><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></span> <a href=\"#/people/ringo-starr/biography/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a></div><p>Ringo Starr was The Beatles&#8217; drummer and occasional singer. He was the oldest member and the last to join the band. <span id=\"more-13\"></span></p><blockquote><div>Ringo&#8217;s a damn good drummer. He was always a good drummer. He&#8217;s not <em>technically</em> good, but I think Ringo&#8217;s drumming is underrated the same way as <a href=\"#/people/paul-mccartney/\">Paul</a>’s bass playing is underrated…</p><p>I think Paul and Ringo stand up anywhere with <em>any</em> of the rock musicians. Not technically great. None of us were technical musicians. None of us could read music. None of us can write it. But as pure musicians, as inspired humans to make noise, they&#8217;re as good as anybody!</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">John Lennon, 1980<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/allwearesaying\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>All We Are Saying</em></a>, David Sheff</div><h2>The early years</h2><p>Ringo was born Richard Starkey on 7 July 1940, at 9 Madryn Street in the Dingle area of Liverpool.</p><p>His mother Elsie (née Gleave) had been born on 19 October 1914. She married Richard Starkey Senior, on 24 October 1936, and they separated in September 1943 when the young Ritchie was 3 years old.</p><p>Elsie remarried Harry Graves (born 1913) on 17 April 1953. Graves got on well with Richard and encouraged the boy&#8217;s passion for music.</p><p>A sickly child, Starkey spent long stretches in hospital. Among his afflictions were a coma caused by appendicitis, a cold which led to pleurisy, and various allergies and intolerances to certain foods. His illnesses made him fall behind academically, and he didn&#8217;t return to school after a stay in hospital which began at the age of 13.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/ringo-starr/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-13 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/ringo-starr-baby_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNTIiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTUyIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"152\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01-152x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr as a baby\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01-152x200.jpg 152w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01-442x580.jpg 442w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01.jpg 640w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 152px) 100vw, 152px\" data-attachment-id=\"20193\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1940s-1950s-photos/ringo-starr-baby_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"640,840\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr as a baby\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr-baby_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNzEiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTcxIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"171\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01-171x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) with his mother Elsie, 1948/9\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01-171x200.jpg 171w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01-495x580.jpg 495w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01.jpg 768w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 171px) 100vw, 171px\" data-attachment-id=\"46775\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"768,900\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) with his mother Elsie, 1948/9\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_01.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNDciIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTQ3IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"147\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-147x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) as a child in the 1940s\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-147x200.jpg 147w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-427x580.jpg 427w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-707x960.jpg 707w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-768x1043.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01.jpg 1080w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 147px) 100vw, 147px\" data-attachment-id=\"46773\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1080,1467\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) as a child in the 1940s\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_01-707x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr_02/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNzYiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTc2IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"176\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02-176x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) as a child in the 1940s\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02-176x200.jpg 176w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02-509x580.jpg 509w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02.jpg 640w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 176px) 100vw, 176px\" data-attachment-id=\"46774\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr_02/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"640,729\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) as a child in the 1940s\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr_02.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzMiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTMzIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"133\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02-133x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) with his mother Elsie, 1940s\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02-133x200.jpg 133w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02-387x580.jpg 387w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02.jpg 640w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 133px) 100vw, 133px\" data-attachment-id=\"46776\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"640,960\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr (Richard Starkey) with his mother Elsie, 1940s\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/40s-ringo-starr-mother-elsie_02-640x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>Known as Ritchie as a teenager, Starkey became infatuated with the skiffle craze which swept Liverpool and elsewhere in the 1950s. He co-founded the Eddie Miles Band, which later became Eddie Clayton and the Clayton Squares, and in 1959 joined the Raving Texans – backing band for local singer Rory Storm.</p><p>It was while playing in these Liverpool bands that he gained the nickname Ringo Starr – the first part due to the rings he wore, and the second because his solos – which Ringo performed reluctantly – could be billed as &#8216;Starr Time&#8217;.</p><h2>With The Beatles</h2><p>Ringo met The Beatles in Hamburg in October 1960. At the time he was performing with Rory Storm and The Hurricanes, but stepped in on a number of occasions when <a href=\"#/people/pete-best/\">Pete Best</a> was unavailable. At the time there was a sense of solidarity among the British groups in Hamburg, and The Beatles got to know Starr well.</p><p>When <a href=\"#/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> demanded that Best be replaced in the summer of 1962, The Beatles insisted that Ringo was the best drummer for them. The decision was controversial among the group&#8217;s fans, who demanded &#8220;Pete forever! Ringo never!&#8221; at the Cavern, and fights broke out.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/ringo-starr/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-2' class='gallery galleryid-13 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/ringo-starr_011/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNjAiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTYwIDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"160\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011-160x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr, 1963\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011-160x200.jpg 160w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011-464x580.jpg 464w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011.jpg 500w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 160px) 100vw, 160px\" data-attachment-id=\"10026\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/ringo-starr_011/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"500,625\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr, 1963\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_011.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/ringo-starr_010/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzYiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM2IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"136\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010-136x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010-136x200.jpg 136w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010-394x580.jpg 394w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010.jpg 612w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 136px) 100vw, 136px\" data-attachment-id=\"10025\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/ringo-starr/ringo-starr_010/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"612,900\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Ringo Starr\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/ringo-starr_010.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>However, Starr didn&#8217;t play drums on The Beatles&#8217; first single, Love Me Do. Martin brought session drummer Andy White in for the session, relegating Starr to tambourine on <a href=\"#/songs/love-me-do/\">&#8216;Love Me Do&#8217;</a>, and maracas on its b-side <a href=\"#/songs/ps-i-love-you/\">&#8216;PS I Love You&#8217;</a>. From then on Ringo played on virtually all The Beatles&#8217; recordings.</p><p>Ringo Starr quickly established himself as a rock-steady drummer, whose open hi-hat and four-to-the-floor bass drum helped energise The Beatles&#8217; sound. He was a reliable performer who made only a handful of mistakes during the band&#8217;s recording career.</p><p>A left-handed drummer who performed on a kit conventionally set up for a right-handed player, Ringo formed a distinctive sound – not least his &#8216;backwards&#8217; fills which were created by leading with the &#8216;wrong&#8217; hand. As Ian MacDonald noted, &#8220;Starr would, during fills, come off the snare onto the tom-toms with his left hand leading so that he could only progress &#8216;backwards&#8217; from floor tom to small tom or from small tom to snare.</p><blockquote><div>His droll variations on this, including rolling off the hi-hat, delighted orthodox drummers and added to the newness of The Beatles&#8217; sound.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Ian MacDonald<br />\n<em>Revolution In The Head</em></div><p>Examples of his characteristic fills can be found on <a href=\"#/songs/a-day-in-the-life/\">&#8216;A Day In The Life&#8217;</a>, <a href=\"#/songs/hey-jude/\">&#8216;Hey Jude&#8217;</a>, and the <a href=\"#/songs/paperback-writer/\">&#8216;Paperback Writer&#8217;</a> b-side <a href=\"#/songs/rain/\">&#8216;Rain&#8217;</a> – which Starr considers to be his best drumming.</p><p>&#8216;Ringoisms&#8217; – expressions coined by Starr and adopted by the band – were used by <a href=\"#/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a> for the titles of <a href=\"#/songs/a-hard-days-night/\">&#8216;A Hard Day&#8217;s Night&#8217;</a> and <a href=\"#/songs/tomorrow-never-knows/\">&#8216;Tomorrow Never Knows&#8217;</a>. He also contributed the line &#8220;Darning his socks in the night&#8221; to <a href=\"#/songs/eleanor-rigby/\">&#8216;Eleanor Rigby&#8217;</a>.</p><p>He became the central character in the films <em>Help!</em> and <em>Yellow Submarine</em> – which were a testament to his popularity as a band member. <em>A Hard Day&#8217;s Night</em>, too, showed his natural ability as an actor, though he subsequently downplayed his performance, claiming he was hungover while shooting his solo scenes.</p><div data-carousel-extra='{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/people/ringo-starr/biography/&quot;}' id='gallery-3' class='gallery galleryid-13 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail'><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1964-photos/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTE5IiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDExOSI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"119\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-200x119.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Ringo Starr in A Hard Day&#039;s Night, 24 April 1964\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-200x119.jpg 200w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-580x345.jpg 580w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-960x570.jpg 960w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-768x456.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01-1536x913.jpg 1536w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/640424-ringo-starr-hard-days-night_01.jpg 1759w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\" dat